{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Virgin daughter of Babylon.</b> The meaning is that she is like a virgin, whose virgin blood has not gone forth." "<b>Daughter.</b> Like Qohelet [i.e., a construct noun used as an appositional epithet]." "<b>No throne.</b> You will not have a throne forever." "<b>And the delicate one.</b> An adjective, like אדומה (Numbers 19:2)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:21.576252227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}